**Assignment** Visual Prompt Studio 1.2: The Immersive Album Cover Challenge
**Prompt** This prompt is somewhat of a Sci-Fi twist on Acoustic Folk / Americana vibes, having a beuatiful forst nd mountain rnage yet have a few lush floating islands to make it feel special and a wonder of nature. My central feature would be the tree to the left of the piece, from my perspective I went for more of a lo-fi/nature white noise album cover designed to calm and relax with, yet still maintaining a sense of wonder and awe. The piece is over all very bright and softly colored making it feel like a safe and calm place to sight see. Although the darker mountains and white fogg still give it a sense of adventure and curiosity. The fore ground has a large tree and river, in which the river slowly becomes smaller, paired with medium sized trees and eventually the mountains which look smll in small but are grand. Due to this the image look straight out of a nature documentary for extoic planet wildlife. The setting sun also adis to show the passing of time in the softer morning/evening light that barely illuminates the wilds. The piece overallholds a very calm and cohessive color pallete with a few pops of color to really bring home the feeling of wonder and awe. This Album cover is definitely not symmetrical but when is a forst landscape ever symmetrical and following the rules. Trees and rocks don't ask permission to exist, they simply do.
**Vocabulary Breakdowns** Value - Value is very importnt as it can make or break a piece, it sets the way a piece is interperted by using light and shadows to enhance its natural lines and colors. Space - The usage of depth perception in a piece to show distance, size, and grandeur. Unity - The glue that holds a piece together, normally classified by color, shape, and texture to make it look cohesive or choatic. Balance - Balance can be perceived in many ways teh symmetry of the piece, the ratio, or the frequency of shapes and colors, either way balance is used to maintain a sense of order or portray a story. Rythym - Rythym is something we often find in songs to make it stick with us and catch our emotions in a vice, for art this also happens, the rythym of a piece is unique and grasps at different people and styles depending on how it is received. By using Colors, Values, Shapes, Patterns, and other means of art attributes.
